# groove.part -- A groove in a floor, ending flush with a lip on it
# Copyright (c) 2026 Jakob Kastelic

# A floor, its top at z = 0, with a lip standing on it at its front, the
# back face of the lip at y = 0, and a groove along y in the floor, its
# walls drafted 1.5 degrees, ending flush with the back of the lip.  The
# inner corners of the groove end get a round of 1.2; the groove edges
# along the floor a round of 0.3, which runs on round the 1.2 rounds and
# ends on the back of the lip, where those rounds run on smoothly into
# it, along a nodal section of its torus.
profile sp along y 0 -10 0 40 -10 0 40 0 0 0 0 0
extrude slab from -5 to 30 sp
profile lp along y 0 0 0 40 0 0 40 5 0 0 5 0
extrude lip from -5 to 0 lp
union body slab lip
profile gp along y 15 -5 0 25 -5 0 25 1 0 15 1 0
extrude groove from 35 to 0 gp draft 1.5
subtract part body groove
round 1.2 lip.end groove
round 0.3 groove slab
round 0.3 slab.end any
